    <h2 class="sec" id="part-e-ph-the-acid-base-scale">Part E · pH — the acid-base scale</h2>

    <div class="content-panel">
      <div class="panel-title">pH 0–14: from battery acid to drain cleaner</div>
      <div class="ph-scale">
        <div class="ph-row"><div class="ph-num-red">0</div><div class="ph-bar-battery-acid"><span class="ph-bar-text-blush">Battery acid, stomach acid (pH ~1.5)</span></div></div>
        <div class="ph-row"><div class="ph-num-red">2</div><div class="ph-bar-lemon"><span class="ph-bar-text-white">Lemon juice (~2.2), vinegar (~2.5)</span></div></div>
        <div class="ph-row"><div class="ph-num-brown">4</div><div class="ph-bar-tomato"><span class="ph-bar-text-dark">Tomato juice (~4), coffee (~5)</span></div></div>
        <div class="ph-row"><div class="ph-num-green">7</div><div class="ph-bar-water"><span class="ph-bar-text-white">Pure water — neutral</span></div></div>
        <div class="ph-row"><div class="ph-num-green">7.4</div><div class="ph-bar-blood"><span class="ph-bar-text-deep-green">Human blood — must stay here</span></div></div>
        <div class="ph-row"><div class="ph-num-blue">9</div><div class="ph-bar-baking-soda"><span class="ph-bar-text-white">Baking soda (~8.3), seawater (~8.1)</span></div></div>
        <div class="ph-row"><div class="ph-num-blue">11</div><div class="ph-bar-ammonia"><span class="ph-bar-text-white">Ammonia (~11), bleach (~12)</span></div></div>
        <div class="ph-row"><div class="ph-num-navy">14</div><div class="ph-bar-drain-cleaner"><span class="ph-bar-text-pale-blue">Drain cleaner, NaOH</span></div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="insight-note">
        <strong class="text-primary">pH is logarithmic.</strong> Each step is 10× more acidic or alkaline. pH 3 is 10× more acidic than pH 4, and 100× more acidic than pH 5. Stomach acid (pH ~1.5) is roughly 30,000× more acidic than blood (pH 7.4). Your body maintains blood pH within ±0.1 of 7.4 — outside pH 6.8 or 7.8, death occurs.
      </div>
    </div>

