    <h2 class="sec" id="part-h-boiling-points-how-structure-determines-state-of-matter">Part H · boiling points — how structure determines state of matter</h2>

    <div class="content-panel">
      <div class="inline-card-title">Same molecular weight, wildly different boiling points</div>
      <div class="section-intro">Molecular weight alone doesn't determine boiling point — intermolecular forces do. Two molecules of similar mass but different functional groups can have boiling points 100°C apart.</div>

